  "worked_solution": "First, we rearrange the equation as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{tan}\u2061(2x-{45}^{\u2218})-\\sqrt{3} & =0 \\\\ \\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{tan}\u2061(2x-{45}^{\u2218}) & =\\sqrt{3} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}\u2061(2x-{45}^{\u2218}) & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{\\sqrt{3}} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}\u2061(2x-{45}^{\u2218}) & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe will find the general solution to the equation, and then generate all of the solutions in the required domain.\n\nThe general solution to our equation is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x-{45}^{\u2218} & ={45}^{\u2218}+n\\cdot {180}^{\u2218}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving our equation for $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x & ={45}^{\u2218}+{45}^{\u2218}+n\\cdot {180}^{\u2218} \\\\ 2x & ={90}^{\u2218}+n\\cdot {180}^{\u2218} \\\\ x & ={45}^{\u2218}+n\\cdot {90}^{\u2218}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe set $n=0,\\pm 1,\\pm 2,\u2026,$ until we have generated all solutions in the domain ${0}^{\u2218}\\le x<{360}^{\u2218}.$\n\n- Setting $n=0$ gives $x={45}^{\u2218}$\n\n- Setting $n=1$ gives $x={135}^{\u2218}$\n\n- Setting $n=2$ gives $x={225}^{\u2218}$\n\n- Setting $n=3$ gives $x={315}^{\u2218}$\n\nAll other values of $n$ generate solutions outside the domain ${0}^{\u2218}\\le x<{360}^{\u2218}.$ So, the solutions ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},{x}_{3}$ and ${x}_{4}$ (written in ascending order) are\n\n$$\nx={45}^{\u2218},{135}^{\u2218},{225}^{\u2218},{315}^{\u2218}.\n$$\n\nFinally, the numerical value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}$ is $45\\cdot 135=6\\,075.$",
